<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL ON 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 91-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills at Monday's auction and all of the 50</p>
<p>million litas issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the</p>
<p>country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 10.40 percent, down from the 10.58</p>
<p>percent offered at the last auction for 91-day paper on April</p>
<p>14.</p>
<p>The settlement date is April 24 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>July 24.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DAYS  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD  LAST AV. YIELD  DEMAND</p>
<p>50    91    9.75/10.76	  10.40	10.58	  92.477</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
</text>
